    "title": "System log files cleared",
    "desc": "A program deleted, truncated or shredded a system log, or vacuumed the systemd journal - wiping /var/log/messages, syslog, secure, auth.log, wtmp/btmp, the audit log or the journal. Destroying the logs that record what happened on the host is a deliberate anti-forensics step after an intrusion (MITRE T1070.002): it removes the evidence a responder would read. history_tamper covers a user's shell history; this covers the host's own logs. A rotate of an application's own log (logrotate truncating /var/log/myapp.log) is not matched; the named system logs are.",
